      "text": "G-START&gt;G-Q0"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:3:81",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "3:81",
        "x": "6591",
        "y": "130",
        "width": "560",
        "height": "213",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "START\nPatient reports hip or knee pain.\nAlready established: the pain is musculoskeletal (bone, joint, muscle, tendon or nerve of the leg) — not coming from the heart, abdomen, skin or another body system."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:3:85",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "3:85",
        "x": "6631",
        "y": "433",
        "width": "480",
        "height": "182",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "Q0 · Where is the main pain?\nASK: \"Point with one finger to where it hurts the most.\"\nWATCH: a hand cupped around the side of the hip (the \"C-sign\") points to the hip joint itself."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:3:89",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "3:89",
        "x": "100",
        "y": "735",
        "width": "280",
        "height": "130",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "At the knee, or just above or below it"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:3:93",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "3:93",
        "x": "13362",
        "y": "735",
        "width": "280",
        "height": "130",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "Groin, side of the hip, buttock or upper thigh"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:3:97",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "3:97",
        "x": "6731",
        "y": "735",
        "width": "280",
        "height": "107",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "Both, or not sure"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "cNyP7TFyrcoIYVPUoQlMgw:3:101",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "3:101",
        "x": "6651",
        "y": "912",
        "width": "440",
        "height": "251",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "Check the HIP first\nHip problems often send pain down to the knee — especially hip osteoarthritis, and a slipped growth plate at the hip in children. If moving the hip (turning it in and out, bent to 90°) reproduces the knee pain, the hip is the source → HIP PATHWAY. If not → KNEE PATHWAY."
    }
  ]
}
